00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:06.080
episode

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:06.080
"The Doll

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:06.080
 that Began to Walk"

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:12.130
Brigadier Oscar François de Jarjayes.

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:14.190
As of April 1st,

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:17.840
you have been appointed as the commanding
officer of the French Guards Company B.

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:20.140
The French Guards Company B...

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:23.690
Furthermore, this is a message
from Lady Antoinette.

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:25.790
''Presently, the only open post
was in the French Guards.''

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:28.500
''If you should object to this,
do say so immediately.''

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:30.140
''Please take care of yourself.''

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:31.120
...is her message.

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:35.340
Please convey this to Lady Antoinette.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:37.810
That I, Oscar François,

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:41.540
am grateful from the bottom of my heart,
for her granting my selfish request.

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:44.740
And to please take care of herself, as well.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:50.150
In honor of the
Regiment Commander of the Royal Guards!

00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:51.310
Right, face!

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:55.450
Present, arms!

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:06.080
Thank you, everyone.

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:07.890
That was my last troops review.

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:10.100
Everything was executed
flawlessly and was splendid.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:14.810
Regiment Commander,
why are you suddenly abandoning us?

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:17.020
It's not that I'm abandoning you.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.420
Have we done something wrong?

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:22.430
Not at all.

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:25.000
You've all done a fine job under me.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.160
I'm really grateful.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:29.000
Girodelle, you've been especially helpful.

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:31.440
That's not an explanation!

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:34.790
Please tell us why you are leaving the
Royal Guards to join the French Guards!

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:37.000
Compared to the Royal Guards,

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.310
the French Guards are a crude regiment of
commoners who are much lower in rank!

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:42.760
We don't want you to transfer to such a place!

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:47.790
Girodelle, I recommended you as my successor.

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:49.180
I leave the rest to you.

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:51.740
Regiment Commander!

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:24.970
André.

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:26.390
Yes?

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:29.130
I'm transferring to the French Guards
a week from today.

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:31.350
Until then, I'll be staying at the villa in Normandy.

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:33.860
You no longer have to accompany me starting today.

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:34.370
You no longer have to accompany me starting today.

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:35.430
Yes.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.340
I'm not angry about what
happened the other day.

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:40.280
I also refuse to let it remain
in my memory though.

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:42.110
<i>Let go of me, André! I'll yell for someone!</i>

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:53.380
<i>Well...?</i>

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:56.540
<i>What are you going to do to me, André...?</i>

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:03.490
<i>I'm sorry...</i>

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:07.190
<i>I swear to God, I'll never do
something like this again.</i>

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:38.960
<i>Oscar thinks to herself about how there
are many different kinds of love.</i>

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:41.400
<i>A love that is requited...</i>

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:43.970
<i>A love where one yearns for it to be requited...</i>

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:46.070
<i>A love that is unrequited
due to one's own actions...</i>

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:48.670
<i>...and yet yearned for by someone unexpected...</i>

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:52.300
<i>A love that goes unnoticed
despite being together...</i>

00:06:53.210 --> 00:06:56.010
<i>The love that André has for her...</i>

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:01.250
<i>It was the same love that Oscar
had once had for Fersen.</i>

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:06.480
<i>For that reason, she knew exactly how
painful it must be for André. Even so...!</i>

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:11.290
<i>''I'll avoid seeing him as much
as possible,'' thought Oscar.</i>

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:15.830
<i>''I'm sorry, André,'' thought Oscar.</i>

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:39.480
Hey, mind if I join you?

00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:41.930
Not at all.

00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:42.440
Go ahead.

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:45.720
Here.

00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:47.730
Thank you.

00:07:54.670 --> 00:07:58.620
I've got a useless leg, but it seems
your eyes are useless, as well.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.180
You're also suffering from love.

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:05.480
Yeah...

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:12.920
People see two kinds of light in this world.

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:15.390
One is the light from the sun and stars.

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:17.900
It's a light, which you can see with your eyes.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:22.000
The other light is the light
of hope in people's hearts.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:26.940
You can't see with just your eyes,
but it's what you need most.

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:28.900
As long as you have this, you can live.

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:31.670
Even if you've hit rock bottom, you can still live.

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:35.180
It's one's heart, Monsieur.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:37.810
Love is between two hearts.

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:42.620
Eyes are nothing but an accessory.

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:48.130
Cheer up.

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:50.490
Cheer up, Monsieur.

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:03.980
So long, Mireille...

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:06.940
Don't be a cheat...

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:14.590
My fist is more frightening
than the enemy's bullets!

00:09:14.590 --> 00:09:19.490
Let's go, let's go. Off to battle I go.

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:25.220
Because a giant brawl is a man's desire!

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:27.670
It's been a while, young fellow!

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:28.460
Hi!

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:31.440
Hey, look at what a sorry place this is.

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:32.670
We're the only customers?

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:33.640
All right!

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:36.840
I'll take you to a better place.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:37.480
Come along!

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:38.450
Hey, Alain!

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:40.240
That's enough already!

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:41.560
We're still on duty!

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:43.560
Damn. They found me.

00:09:45.820 --> 00:09:46.970
Well, there you have it.

00:09:46.970 --> 00:09:48.400
Let's save it for a later date.

00:09:50.260 --> 00:09:51.190
You moron.

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:52.290
Quit being such a do-gooder.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:54.650
But we're on special alert tonight!

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:55.590
Fine.

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:56.830
Back to work.

00:09:56.830 --> 00:09:57.530
Wait!

00:09:57.530 --> 00:09:58.620
Hold on!

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:02.580
Alain, you're in the French Guards... right?

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:04.300
Yeah, Company B.

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:05.830
Company B...!

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:07.790
What about it?

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:10.260
I need to ask you for a favor!

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:17.810
French Guards' Barracks

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:16.950
Come in!

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:25.590
I am Colonel d'Agout,
Lieutenant Commander of Company B.

00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:27.150
I look forward to working with you!

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:29.100
And I, as well.

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:34.470
Anyhow, I was told your inaugural troops
review would take place tomorrow.

00:10:34.470 --> 00:10:36.030
It seems you're a day early.

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:38.570
Yes, this is my first time in the French Guards,

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:41.240
so I wanted to familiarize myself
and figured the sooner the better.

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:43.070
Please take me to the soldiers' barracks.

00:10:43.070 --> 00:10:44.120
W-Well...

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:46.240
Nice hand!

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:48.920
Sorry, better luck next time.

00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:52.580
I feel rather uneasy about taking our newly appointed
commander to such a distasteful place...

00:10:52.580 --> 00:10:53.550
I don't mind.

00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:03.430
Hey, guys! The new commander is coming!

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:05.100
What?!

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:05.900
Hey, all of you!

00:11:06.460 --> 00:11:08.460
Come on, hurry!

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:11.940
What a pain. Why out of the blue?

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:12.760
Sheesh!

00:11:17.810 --> 00:11:18.570
Please!

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:27.880
Starting tomorrow, I will be your Commander.

00:11:28.460 --> 00:11:30.790
I am Oscar François de Jarjayes.
I look forward to working with you all.

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:39.840
All men! Salute our new commander!

00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:51.240
What is the meaning of this, André?!

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:53.400
I told you not to accompany me anymore!

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:55.580
I'm not accompanying you, Oscar.

00:11:55.580 --> 00:11:57.140
I'm a member of this unit.

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:01.860
I have an acquaintance in this unit,
so I joined through him yesterday.

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:05.060
No matter what happens...
No matter what you think of me...

00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:06.660
I'm the only one who can protect you.

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:10.320
I'll be leaving now, Commander!

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:14.290
André!

00:12:19.140 --> 00:12:20.470
Do whatever you want...!

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:28.400
Hey, did you hear about our new commander?

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:31.460
Prepare to be amazed.

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:34.130
The uniform hides it well, but our
commander is really a woman!

00:12:34.130 --> 00:12:35.510
What? Are you pulling our leg?

00:12:35.510 --> 00:12:37.110
Our Commander is a woman?

00:12:37.510 --> 00:12:38.450
You've got to be kidding me!

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:40.200
I'm not going to put up with that.

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:42.310
There's no way I'm taking orders from a woman.

00:12:42.310 --> 00:12:43.310
Hey, Alain!

00:12:43.310 --> 00:12:44.110
What do you think?

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:46.570
Well...

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:48.830
I'm not amused that's for sure.

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:18.120
Hey, André. Wake up!

00:13:18.580 --> 00:13:20.070
It's time for you to be on watch.

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:24.820
There we go.

00:13:25.690 --> 00:13:27.950
Just relax. Nothing's gonna happen{ is going to happen anyway}.

00:13:29.960 --> 00:13:31.860
Well, even if something were to happen,

00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:35.350
it'll be the citizens of Paris sneaking
in to steal the unit's food at most.

00:13:37.300 --> 00:13:39.420
Sit down, Monsieur ''Carpenter's Son.''

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:43.800
You told me you were a carpenter's son, right?

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:47.720
And that you wanted to join the French Guards, so you asked me to help you.

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:49.280
Well, never mind that.

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:50.440
Why did you lie?

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:52.950
Tell me the reason.

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:54.020
I don't have any reason.

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:55.450
Plus, I didn't lie.

00:13:55.450 --> 00:13:56.420
Quit it.

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:58.350
You're no son of a carpenter.

00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:02.780
I hate nobles and you smell like one.

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:10.330
I'm not a noble.

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:11.830
I never said you were.

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:13.830
I only said you smell like one.

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:18.330
Someone saw you being called into
that new commander's office.

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:21.340
Well, no matter.

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:24.110
Everyone has their reasons for
not wanting to tell others.

00:14:24.110 --> 00:14:26.250
But let me tell you this, André.

00:14:26.250 --> 00:14:30.350
The French Guards is crawling with men
who hate nobles, much more than I do.

00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:35.980
Even worse, if it's a snobbish
blue-blooded woman.

00:14:43.260 --> 00:14:46.920
My Lady, you'll be working in the French Guards starting today, correct?

00:14:47.410 --> 00:14:49.270
So, um...

00:14:49.270 --> 00:14:49.970
Well...

00:14:49.970 --> 00:14:51.040
What is it?

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:53.280
Well, it's about André...

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:56.410
I haven't seen him for three days now.

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:59.040
I thought perhaps you might know something...?

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:01.120
He probably won't be back for a while.

00:15:01.120 --> 00:15:03.420
André is living in the barracks now.

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:06.510
Huh? What do you mean?

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:12.030
Don't worry, Nanna.

00:15:12.030 --> 00:15:14.130
André is André. I am me.

00:15:14.130 --> 00:15:15.310
We're no longer children.

00:15:15.630 --> 00:15:16.570
Yes...

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:28.490
Come in.

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:31.450
Commander, everyone is gathered
in the parade ground!

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:33.880
Please take part in your inaugural troops review.

00:15:52.170 --> 00:15:53.640
How could this be?!

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:56.430
They were all gathered here just a moment ago!

00:16:05.180 --> 00:16:05.820
André.

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:09.780
Every man in Company B refuses to take
part in your inaugural troops review.

00:16:10.760 --> 00:16:12.240
Why? Tell me the reason.

00:16:12.660 --> 00:16:15.200
They said they don't want to take
orders from a female commander.

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:20.330
If the troops review is cancelled, I'd also
like to go back to the barracks...

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:21.830
Of course, it's cancelled!

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:24.960
How are we supposed to have a troops
review with just one soldier!

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:25.860
Excuse me then.

00:16:30.470 --> 00:16:31.240
Bull's-eye!

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:32.380
Not bad.

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:34.410
All right, let me try this time!

00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:35.350
Sure, go ahead.

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:47.320
You should know better, Commander.

00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:48.900
You should knock before you enter.

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:58.790
Wh-What?!

00:16:58.790 --> 00:17:00.670
Knock on the door, you say?

00:17:00.670 --> 00:17:03.330
People who have manners only
deserve to say such things!

00:17:05.720 --> 00:17:07.510
You skipped out on the troops review!

00:17:07.510 --> 00:17:10.090
It's hardly believable that you
have manners of any sort!

00:17:10.510 --> 00:17:11.450
All right, men!

00:17:11.450 --> 00:17:13.450
Button up and get yourselves
out to the parade ground!

00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:14.260
We're doing the troops review!

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:20.850
They're all saying they don't want to.

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:25.840
Why don't you go back to the Royal Guards?

00:17:25.840 --> 00:17:29.240
Our unit doesn't have any men of refinement,
who'll listen to a female commander's orders.

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:33.480
If you have something to say, get out
of bed and say it like a man!

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:34.710
This isn't a hospital!

00:17:35.210 --> 00:17:36.700
Oh, pardon my manners.

00:17:39.420 --> 00:17:42.820
To add to that, this is Company B. We have
a reputation for being especially rough.

00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:45.170
None of us wants to see you get injured, you see...

00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:49.260
Just so you know, I don't mind rough tactics.

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:52.140
In fact, I'd like to see just
how rough you really are.

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:53.630
Oh?

00:17:53.930 --> 00:17:55.020
What did you say?!

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:56.500
Look who's talking!

00:17:56.500 --> 00:17:59.340
Sounds interesting! We'll show you then!

00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:01.310
All right, it's settled then.

00:18:01.310 --> 00:18:03.570
Anyone confident in their fighting skills
should come to the parade ground!

00:18:03.570 --> 00:18:05.270
Guns, swords... Take your pick!

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:21.080
Alain, you always represent us.

00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:22.280
We're counting on you.

00:18:22.280 --> 00:18:24.670
Rough her up real good for us!

00:18:25.060 --> 00:18:27.700
Sorry, but count me out this time.

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:29.630
Taking on a woman isn't my thing.

00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:31.100
You do it!

00:18:31.900 --> 00:18:33.700
R-Really?!

00:18:33.700 --> 00:18:34.640
All right!

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:36.810
Let's go, everyone!

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:37.720
To the parade ground!

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:50.220
Are we clear?!

00:18:50.220 --> 00:18:52.420
If I win, we do the troops review!

00:18:52.420 --> 00:18:54.910
If I lose, I'll leave the French Guards immediately!

00:18:55.990 --> 00:18:57.110
Now you're talking.

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:05.710
Whoa!

00:19:11.740 --> 00:19:12.800
I see.

00:19:12.800 --> 00:19:14.650
No wonder you've earned a
reputation for being rough.

00:19:14.650 --> 00:19:15.510
You're quite skilled.

00:19:21.010 --> 00:19:21.770
Damn it!

00:19:35.530 --> 00:19:36.620
It's settled.

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:41.910
Why you...!

00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:58.170
Damn bitch!

00:19:58.820 --> 00:19:59.640
Get her!

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:02.000
Wait!

00:20:03.460 --> 00:20:04.530
Wait up.

00:20:04.530 --> 00:20:05.790
Everyone, wait up.

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:08.700
A promise is a promise.

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:10.470
We lost.

00:20:10.470 --> 00:20:12.650
Let's just do the troops review.

00:20:14.740 --> 00:20:15.440
Damn.

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:16.810
All right, Alain.

00:20:16.810 --> 00:20:18.810
If you say so, fine then.

00:20:18.810 --> 00:20:20.810
Just so we're clear, Commander...!

00:20:20.810 --> 00:20:24.070
Don't think that we've accepted you.

00:20:24.850 --> 00:20:25.780
I understand.

00:20:26.380 --> 00:20:28.220
And one more thing.

00:20:28.220 --> 00:20:30.290
This is basic stuff, but...

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:35.250
We're not in the military to protect the nobles,
let alone protect the royal palace.

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:38.960
Frankly, we're doing it for the pay.

00:20:38.960 --> 00:20:40.060
So we can eat!

00:20:40.060 --> 00:20:41.670
Just remember that.

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:45.470
Right, face!

00:21:16.730 --> 00:21:18.840
Welcome back, My Lady.

00:21:21.510 --> 00:21:23.010
A guest? For me?

00:21:23.010 --> 00:21:25.970
Yes, he's been waiting for you
since early this evening.

00:21:34.380 --> 00:21:36.110
It's been a while, Regiment Commander.

00:21:37.920 --> 00:21:40.060
Oh, it's you, Girodelle!

00:21:40.060 --> 00:21:41.190
Why the sudden visit?

00:21:41.190 --> 00:21:43.030
Is there something troubling
you at the Royal Guards?

00:21:43.330 --> 00:21:47.710
No, I've come to make a personal request
to your father, General Jarjayes, today.

00:21:48.130 --> 00:21:49.230
My father?

00:21:49.230 --> 00:21:50.200
I see.

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:51.140
Well, it's been a while.

00:21:51.140 --> 00:21:52.700
How about some wine?

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:53.440
Nanna!

00:21:53.440 --> 00:21:54.740
No, I'll be leaving now.

00:21:54.740 --> 00:21:57.000
What? But I was told you were waiting for me.

00:21:58.440 --> 00:21:59.240
Yes.

00:21:59.780 --> 00:22:03.550
But seeing your smile was enough for me tonight.

00:22:03.550 --> 00:22:04.720
Perhaps some other time.

00:22:11.020 --> 00:22:14.320
Nanna, what did Girodelle come here for?

00:22:14.320 --> 00:22:18.000
Lord Girodelle said this to Master,

00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:20.610
''Please allow me to marry your daughter.''

00:22:21.430 --> 00:22:22.270
What...?!

00:22:22.270 --> 00:22:23.730
And the Master's reply was,

00:22:23.730 --> 00:22:28.230
''What a splendid proposal!
You have my blessing!''

00:22:28.660 --> 00:22:33.500
To be continued

